OL,3,GNEWSALorry-damaged bridge fully reopens
OL,4,Aafter work
OL,5,
OL,6,FA bridge damaged after a lorry driver
OL,7,Fsmashed the vehicle over part of it has
OL,8,Fbeen fully repaired and reopened.
OL,10,FThe lorry struck the bridge on Church
OL,11,FRoad in Swallowfield, Berkshire, on 11
OL,12,FFebruary, bringing one side of the
OL,13,Fbrick wall down and forcing the road to
OL,14,Fclose for more than two weeks.
OL,16,FDaniel Gowers, 33, from Havering, was
OL,17,Fconvicted of driving without due care
OL,18,Fand attention in his absence in
OL,19,FSeptember. He was fined #1,100 and told
OL,20,Fto pay a #440 surcharge and #130 in
OL,21,Fcosts at Reading Magistrates' Court.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
